1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,320
Level one, the drowning man.

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:07,160
You are 38 years old. You sit at your

3
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:09,560
kitchen table at 2:00 in the morning.

4
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:11,840
The house is quiet. Your wife is asleep

5
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:14,640
upstairs. Your daughter is asleep down

6
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:16,520
the hall. She is 8 years old. She still

7
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:19,000
leaves the hall light on.

8
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:21,600
In front of you are the bills, red ink,

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,600
final notices, a stack of envelopes you

10
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,680
stopped opening weeks ago.

11
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:28,240
You own a small construction business.

12
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:30,520
You owned it is closer to the truth.

13
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:33,280
Now, it owns you.

14
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:35,640
A bad contract that went wrong, a client

15
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:38,200
who never paid, a loan you signed with

16
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:41,400
your house as collateral. The math does

17
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:44,080
not work. It has not worked for a year.

18
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:45,920
You owe more than you will ever earn.

19
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:48,800
The bank sent another letter,

20
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:50,520
foreclosure, 60 days.

21
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,440
You have not told your wife how bad it

22
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:55,760
is. You have been lying to her for

23
00:00:52,440 --> 00:00:58,480
months. Small lies at first, then bigger

24
00:00:55,760 --> 00:01:00,920
ones. Everything is fine. We are getting

25
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:02,320
through it. The lies are getting harder

26
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:04,480
to tell.

27
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:06,480
You stare at your life insurance policy,

28
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:08,880
$400,000.

29
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:10,680
It has sat in a drawer for years. You

30
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:13,080
bought it when your daughter was born, a

31
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:16,000
responsible thing to do, a father thing

32
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:17,480
to do. You never thought about it again

33
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,840
until tonight.

34
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:22,760
Tonight, you think about it differently.

35
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:25,600
Dead men do not owe money to anyone.

36
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:27,440
Dead men are worth $400,000 to the

37
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:29,520
people they leave behind.

38
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:31,400
The thought arrives quietly, without

39
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:33,800
warning. It does not feel like a

40
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:36,360
decision at all. It feels like a door

41
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:38,760
opening in a wall you thought was solid.

42
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:40,880
You tell yourself it is insane. You tell

43
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:44,000
yourself you would never.

44
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:45,960
You go up to bed. You do not sleep. The

45
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,120
thought is still there in the morning.

46
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:50,760
It is there again the next night. It

47
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:54,400
grows a little each time. It has weight

48
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:56,440
now. It has a shape you can almost hold.

49
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:57,840
You start doing something you swore you

50
00:01:56,440 --> 00:02:00,880
would never do.

51
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:03,360
You start to plan.

52
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:05,880
Level two, the planner.

53
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:07,000
The plan needs research. Research leaves

54
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:08,560
a trail.

55
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,440
You cannot look any of this up on your

56
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:11,560
home computer. You know that much

57
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:13,160
already.

58
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:14,720
Search history is the first thing

59
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:16,000
investigators pull when a man goes

60
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:17,520
missing.

61
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,120
So, you drive to the public library

62
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:21,320
across town.

63
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:22,880
You use a machine in the corner.

64
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:24,200
You learn a word for the thing you are

65
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:25,720
considering.

66
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:27,640
Pseudocide.

67
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:29,640
Faking your own death.

68
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:31,120
People have done it for centuries.

69
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:32,160
Some do it for insurance money, like

70
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:34,080
you.

71
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:35,280
Some do it to escape a debt they cannot

72
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:37,480
pay.

73
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:41,640
Some do it to escape a marriage, or a

74
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:43,600
crime, or simply themselves.

75
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:45,440
You read about the men who got caught.

76
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:47,600
You study their mistakes.

77
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:50,120
That is the whole key to this. You do

78
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:51,959
not learn from the ones who succeeded.

79
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:53,120
The ones who succeeded, you never hear

80
00:02:51,959 --> 00:02:54,840
about.

81
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:56,680
You learn everything from the failures

82
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:59,800
instead.

83
00:02:56,680 --> 00:03:01,320
The first mistake is always greed.

84
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:03,519
The man who fakes his death and then

85
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:05,280
files the claim himself.

86
00:03:03,519 --> 00:03:06,800
The man whose wife buys a new car a

87
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:08,600
month later.

88
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:10,280
Insurance companies do not pay that

89
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:11,760
without questions.

90
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:12,880
They hire their own investigators to

91
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:14,920
check.

92
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:17,280
They look for a body.

93
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:18,360
No body means no death certificate gets

94
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:21,239
signed.

95
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:23,680
No death certificate means no payout.

96
00:03:21,239 --> 00:03:26,080
That is the first problem to solve.

97
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:27,480
You need to die with no body, but no

98
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:30,000
doubt.

99
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:32,959
Water is the answer to both.

100
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,920
Water swallows men and keeps them.

101
00:03:32,959 --> 00:03:36,880
Drownings where the body is never found

102
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:39,320
happen all the time.

103
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:41,160
A boating accident on a bad day.

104
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:42,360
A swim in a current stronger than it

105
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:44,519
looked.

106
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:47,480
You live near the coast already.

107
00:03:44,519 --> 00:03:50,400
You own a small boat the marina knows.

108
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:52,480
The pieces start to fit together.

109
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:53,760
The second mistake is staying too close

110
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:56,800
home.

111
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:58,600
Men who fake it and hide one town over.

112
00:03:56,800 --> 00:04:00,080
Men who watch their own funeral from the

113
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:02,280
back.

114
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:03,560
Men who call their wife from a payphone

115
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:05,000
because they miss the sound of her

116
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:07,520
voice.

117
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,680
Every one of them gets caught.

118
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:12,800
You will have to go far away.

119
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:14,720
You will have to go completely.

120
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:16,079
The third mistake is the new identity

121
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:18,079
itself.

122
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:20,519
You cannot just pick a name.

123
00:04:18,079 --> 00:04:22,640
You need real documents behind it.

124
00:04:20,519 --> 00:04:23,720
A birth certificate, a social security

125
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:26,720
number.

126
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:29,120
A history that holds up when checked.

127
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:31,040
You read how men have done it before.

128
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:32,360
Stolen identities that once belonged to

129
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:34,360
the dead.

130
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:35,960
Children who died young and were never

131
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:38,000
closed out.

132
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:40,600
All of it is illegal.

133
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:42,200
You are past caring about that.

134
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:43,200
You fill a notebook with everything you

135
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:45,000
learn.

136
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:46,400
You hide it under a loose floorboard in

137
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:49,160
the garage.

138
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:51,200
You are not a desperate man anymore.

139
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:53,160
You are a man with a plan.

140
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:55,400
And that frightens you more than the

141
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:56,600
debt ever did.

142
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:58,120
Level three,

143
00:04:56,600 --> 00:05:00,640
the stager.

144
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:03,080
Now you have to build the death itself.

145
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:04,720
You give yourself 6 weeks. You act

146
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:06,480
completely normal.

147
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:07,840
That is the hardest part.

148
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:09,040
You eat breakfast with your daughter

149
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:11,000
every morning.

150
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:13,200
You help her with homework. You kiss

151
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:15,680
your wife goodbye each day.

152
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:17,880
You are really memorizing them.

153
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:20,560
You do not tell them any of this. You

154
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:21,800
cannot tell them anything. Your wife can

155
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:23,320
never know.

156
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:25,640
This is the part that keeps you awake at

157
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:26,919
night. If she knows, she becomes a

158
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:28,960
conspirator.

159
00:05:26,919 --> 00:05:30,160
If she knows, the investigators will

160
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:32,520
break her.

161
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:33,600
She is a good woman. She was never good

162
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:35,720
at lying.

163
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:37,320
So you make the hardest choice.

164
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:38,240
You decide that she has to believe it,

165
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:40,280
too.

166
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:43,040
Your own wife will have to bury an empty

167
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:45,400
coffin and mean every tear.

168
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:47,440
You tell yourself it is a gift. She gets

169
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:50,000
the money to clean up the mess. She gets

170
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:52,160
a fresh start without a failing husband.

171
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:55,040
She gets a dead hero instead of a living

172
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:57,120
failure. You almost believe it.

173
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:59,560
You prepare the scene in advance. You

174
00:05:57,120 --> 00:06:01,760
take the boat out every weekend. You

175
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:03,280
build a routine people will remember.

176
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:06,520
The neighbors watch you leave with your

177
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:08,640
gear. The marina logs each trip. You are

178
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:10,040
building a story before you will ever

179
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:12,200
need to tell it.

180
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:14,720
You buy the small things slowly. A

181
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:17,880
prepaid phone paid for in cash.

182
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:19,960
Cash amounts too small to trip alarms. A

183
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:22,080
duffel bag in a storage unit under a

184
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:25,200
name almost yours.

185
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:27,360
Inside that bag is another whole life.

186
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:30,240
Clothes a different man would wear.

187
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:32,640
Money folded and banded. The first fake

188
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:35,400
documents you managed to buy. You drive

189
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:37,800
4 hours to get them. You pay a man cash

190
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:40,600
in a parking lot. You do not ask him his

191
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:42,600
name. He does not ask you yours.

192
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:45,040
You choose the date carefully. A

193
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:47,400
Saturday in October. The water will be

194
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:49,280
cold enough to kill. The current past

195
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:51,560
the point will be brutal.

196
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:53,760
A man who goes into that water does not

197
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:54,880
come out. That is what everyone will

198
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:58,600
believe.

199
00:06:54,880 --> 00:07:00,919
You write no note. A note is evidence. A

200
00:06:58,600 --> 00:07:02,880
note can be analyzed.

201
00:07:00,919 --> 00:07:05,480
You will go out one morning and never

202
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:07,080
come back. The night before you tuck

203
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:09,600
your daughter into bed.

204
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:12,200
You read her two stories instead of one.

205
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:14,880
She asks why she gets an extra one. You

206
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:17,080
say because you love her. She falls

207
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:19,840
asleep before you finish reading. You

208
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:22,400
sit in the dark and almost stop. You

209
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:24,720
almost tear the whole plan down. But the

210
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:27,680
bills are still sitting in the drawer.

211
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:30,960
And the door in the wall is still open.

212
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:33,840
In the morning you go to the water.

213
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:36,000
Level four. The vanishing.

214
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:38,320
You take the boat out just after dawn.

215
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:40,600
The marina is empty at that hour. You

216
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:42,640
wave to the old man always there. He

217
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:45,200
waves back at you without thinking. He

218
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:46,800
will remember that small wave later.

219
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:48,880
He will tell investigators you seemed

220
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:49,920
normal. That is what you needed him to

221
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:51,920
say.

222
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:53,840
You motor out past the point. You go

223
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:56,320
until the land is gone. You have

224
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:58,120
practiced this a hundred times. You drop

225
00:07:56,320 --> 00:08:00,200
the anchor. You leave your wallet

226
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:02,880
sitting on the seat, your phone beside

227
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:05,400
it. Your jacket folded over the rail.

228
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:07,760
Your shoes lined up neatly. It all looks

229
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:10,000
like a man who fell overboard. You leave

230
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:12,280
the engine idling. You leave a fishing

231
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:14,480
line trailing in the water. The scene

232
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:17,000
has to tell the story without you.

233
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:18,800
Then you slip over the side into a raft

234
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:20,640
you hid the night before.

235
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:23,040
You paddle hard toward empty shore,

236
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:24,600
three miles down the coast. Your legs

237
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:27,040
shake the whole way.

238
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:28,960
The water is as cold as you feared.

239
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:31,280
You reach the beach and drag the raft up

240
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:32,560
the sand. You deflate it and bury it in

241
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:34,240
the dunes.

242
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:35,599
You walk the last mile to the storage

243
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:37,880
unit alone.

244
00:08:35,599 --> 00:08:39,000
You open the door and become the other

245
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:40,880
man.

246
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:43,880
New clothes that do not fit quite right

247
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:46,720
yet. A new name you whisper to yourself.

248
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:49,040
A car with plates tracing to nobody.

249
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:51,400
You drive away without a destination.

250
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:53,560
You do not look back once. You do not

251
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:55,280
turn on the radio all day.

252
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:56,680
You do not want to hear a report about a

253
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:59,920
missing boater.

254
00:08:56,680 --> 00:09:01,640
By nightfall, you are 300 miles away.

255
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:04,120
You sleep in a motel that takes only

256
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:06,440
cash. You lie on the bed and stare at

257
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:08,760
the ceiling. Somewhere behind you, the

258
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:10,720
Coast Guard drags the water. Somewhere

259
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:13,320
behind you, a deputy knocks on your

260
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:16,000
door. Somewhere behind you, your wife

261
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:17,640
answers and confusion becomes fear,

262
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:20,280
becomes grief.

263
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:22,640
You did that to her. You put that grief

264
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:24,320
on her face with your own hands.

265
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:25,520
Your daughter is being told her father

266
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:27,720
is gone.

267
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:30,080
You will never see her cry over it. You

268
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:31,800
will never hold her while she does.

269
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:34,240
You wanted this badly enough to spend

270
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:36,920
six weeks building it. Now that it is

271
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:39,000
real, it does not feel like freedom.

272
00:09:36,920 --> 00:09:40,640
It feels like drowning with your lungs

273
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:42,920
still full of air.

274
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:45,040
The man you used to be is dead.

275
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:46,400
You killed him yourself out there.

276
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:47,680
Now you have to be someone else

277
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:51,240
entirely.

278
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:54,160
You have no earthly idea how.

279
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:55,760
Level five, the reborn.

280
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:58,320
You settle in a city where nobody knows

